eld/id #uuid "f9ab268e-f2ec-5625-bfef-8a79c6ffdad3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id 17592186482707}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "89b80d96-a645-5980-81bc-fd0319be6dc0" :question/problem "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(-2,5)$ and is parallel to the line passing through the points $(3,-1)$ and $(6, 5)$. Write your answer in **standard form.** Use $Ax+By=C$ with integer $A,B,C$, $A>0$, and coprime $A$ and $B$ (their greatest common divisor is $1$). Enter $Ax+By$ in the first blank and $C$ in the second blank.\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, let's find the slope of the line passing through the points $(3,-1)$ and $(6,5)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m &= \\frac{y_2-y_1}{x_2-x_1} \\\\ &= \\frac{5-(-1)}{6-(3)} \\\\ &= 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of $2$ and passes through the point $(-2,5)$. To find the equation of this line, we use point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 &= m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(5) &= 2(x-(-2)) \\\\ y-(5) &= 2 x + 4 \\\\ y &= 2 x + 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, write the equation in standard form with coprime integer coefficients and a positive $x$-coefficient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2 x + 9 \\\\ 2 x -y &= -9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first blank is $2 x -y$ and the second blank is $-9$."} {:db/id 17592186482684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "513484e6-7d22-5022-8ecf-85438c0cb103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186482668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "513484e6-7d22-5022-8ecf-85438c0cb103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id 17592186482668} :answer-field/id #uuid "7777689b-2adf-51ef-a25d-24706fb56687" :answer-field/key "field-2" 